│  ├─ vite.config.ts
│  └─ src/
│     ├─ App.tsx
│     ├─ api.ts
│     ├─ main.tsx
│     └─ styles.css
├─ configs/
│  ├─ base.yaml
│  └─ usecases/
│     └─ contracts.yaml
├─ src/
│  ├─ app/
│  ├─ core/
│  ├─ indexing/
│  ├─ rag/
│  └─ storage/
└─ tests/
```

## Run With Docker

```powershell
Copy-Item .env.example .env
docker compose up --build
```

This starts:

- Backend API: `http://127.0.0.1:8000`
- Frontend: `http://127.0.0.1:5173`
- Qdrant: `http://127.0.0.1:6333`

## Run Locally

Backend:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn src.app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
```

Frontend:

```powershell
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

The frontend proxies `/v1` requests to the backend during development. By default it targets `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.

## Environment

Important variables:

- `FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173`
- `VECTOR_STORE_URL=...`
- `QDRANT_API_KEY=...`
- `QDRANT_COLLECTION=rag_chunks`
- `DOC_STORE_URL=sqlite:///./data/rag.db`
- `EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`
- `EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=384`
- `OPENAI_API_KEY=...`

Frontend API target:

- `VITE_API_BASE_URL=` for direct browser calls when needed
- `VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000` for Vite dev proxy

## Current Capabilities

- Upload `.txt`, `.md`, and `.pdf` files
- View indexed files in the frontend
- Delete individual files or clear the full index
- Hybrid retrieval using SQLite FTS5 BM25 plus Qdrant vector search
- Generate answers with retrieved context

## PDF Extraction

- PDF uploads are parsed with Docling before chunking and indexing.
- If `docling` is not installed in the backend environment, PDF uploads will fail with a clear error message.

## Notes

- The backend is API-only and CORS allows the configured frontend origin.
- If you change embedding models, clear and rebuild the index.
- If OpenAI quota is unavailable, generation will fail even when retrieval succeeds.
